        "title": "Count the squares",
        "body": "The longest side of a given piece is 6, so Bob's square has side at least 6 and at least $6\\times6=36$ small squares. The three given pieces have $8+10+6=24$ squares, so the fourth has at least $36-24=12$. Both D and E have 12 squares. Trying them, only E (4 squares wide and 3 high) fits with the other three to make a $6\\times6$ square.\n\n**Answer: (E)**"
